(Quantum Teleportation Experiment Report) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 780 Tm
() Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 765 Tm
(1. Objective) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 750 Tm
(This report describes a complete implementation of the standard single-qubit quantum) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 735 Tm
(teleportation protocol using pyqpanda3. The state to be teleported is |psi> =) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 720 Tm
(cos\(pi/6\)|0> + sin\(pi/6\)|1>. The protocol transfers this unknown state from Alice to Bob) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 705 Tm
(by using a shared Bell pair, Alice's joint measurement, two classical bits, and Bob's) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 690 Tm
(conditional correction gates.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 675 Tm
() Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 660 Tm
(2. Bell-state preparation) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 645 Tm
(The function prepare_bell_state\(q1, q2\) returns a pyqpanda3 QCircuit. It first applies) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 630 Tm
(H\(q1\), which transforms q1 into \(|0> + |1>\) / sqrt\(2\). It then applies CNOT\(q1, q2\). The) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 615 Tm
(resulting two-qubit state is \(|00> + |11>\) / sqrt\(2\), where q1 is Alice's entangled) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 600 Tm
(qubit and q2 is Bob's entangled qubit.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 585 Tm
() Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 570 Tm
(3. Teleportation circuit construction) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 555 Tm
(The function teleportation_circuit\(q0, q1, q2\) builds the whole protocol.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 540 Tm
(Step 1: prepare the unknown state on q0. In pyqpanda3, RY\(theta\)|0> = cos\(theta/2\)|0> +) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 525 Tm
(sin\(theta/2\)|1>. Therefore theta = pi/3 prepares cos\(pi/6\)|0> + sin\(pi/6\)|1>.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 510 Tm
(Step 2: call prepare_bell_state\(q1, q2\) to create the shared Bell state.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 495 Tm
(Step 3: Alice applies CNOT\(q0, q1\) and H\(q0\), then measures q0 into classical bit c0 and) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 480 Tm
(q1 into classical bit c1.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 465 Tm
(Step 4: Bob applies X\(q2\) if c1 = 1 and applies Z\(q2\) if c0 = 1. These conditional) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 450 Tm
(corrections are implemented with pyqpanda3 qif classical-control blocks.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 435 Tm
() Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 420 Tm
(4. Fidelity verification method) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 405 Tm
(After running the circuit on CPUQVM, the script reads the final state vector. pyqpanda3) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 390 Tm
(uses little-endian indexing for state-vector basis states, so the code extracts Bob's) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 375 Tm
(one-qubit state from the bit position of q2. For pure states, the fidelity is computed) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 360 Tm
(as F = |<psi|phi>|^2, where |psi> is the original state and |phi> is Bob's recovered) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 345 Tm
(state after correction. A global phase is removed before displaying amplitudes, because) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 330 Tm
(it has no physical effect.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 315 Tm
() Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 60 300 Tm
